@import com.example.septic.web.PageMeta
@param PageMeta page = null
@param boolean production = false
@template.studio.shell(page = page, production = production, title = "Real record investigations", heroImage = "/images/studio/work-archive-v2.webp", pageClass = "studio-work", pageStyles = "/studio-work.css", mobileHeroImage = "/images/studio/work-archive-mobile-v3.webp", content = @`
<main id="main">
    <section class="studio-hero editorial-hero work-hero" aria-labelledby="work-title"><picture class="editorial-hero__picture"><source media="(max-width: 700px)" srcset="/images/studio/work-archive-mobile-v3.webp"><img class="studio-hero__image" src="/images/studio/work-archive-v2.webp" alt="" width="1672" height="941" fetchpriority="high"></picture><div class="studio-hero__shade"></div><div class="studio-wrap studio-hero__inner"><div class="studio-hero__copy"><p class="studio-overline">Our work / Real record investigations</p><h1 id="work-title">Research.<br>Judgment.<br>A clearer answer.</h1><p class="studio-hero__intro">Online clues. Focused agency questions.<br>Evidence interpreted, and the result delivered.</p><a class="studio-button" href="#sale-case">Explore the work <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div></div></section>
    <section class="editorial-intro studio-wrap" id="sale-case" aria-labelledby="case-title"><div><p class="studio-overline">Shelby County, Tennessee / Sale preparation</p><h2 id="case-title">A missing file.<br>A documented starting point.</h2></div><div><p>A property owner needed a septic file to share with a buyer. Public searches did not supply the missing plan.</p><p>We followed the county route and obtained the source packet. Open the actual plan below to trace the findings to the source; identifying details are omitted.</p></div></section>
    <section class="studio-process" aria-labelledby="trace-title"><div class="studio-wrap"><p class="studio-overline">The work behind the answer</p><h2 id="trace-title">The research behind the handoff.</h2><ol class="work-trace"><li><span>01</span><h3>Find the useful online clues.</h3><p>The plat helped identify the lot but did not show the property's septic installation. An empty public search did not prove that the county held nothing.</p></li><li><span>02</span><h3>Turn the gap into a focused request.</h3><p>After an outdated contact failed, we used the current published route with parcel and lot references. The county returned the permitted site plan.</p></li><li><span>03</span><h3>Close the documentary question.</h3><p>The original three-page county file and a one-page Record Brief were delivered for the buyer conversation. We also passed on the later agency clarification, separating what the file answered from what still needed field verification.</p></li></ol><p class="studio-fine">This documents a records delivery, not a completed sale or a passed inspection. The county found no repair permits or soil/perc records in its file; that does not establish that no repairs ever occurred.</p></div></section>
    <section class="work-evidence" aria-labelledby="evidence-title"><figure class="work-source-gallery"><p class="studio-overline">Read the handwritten specifications</p><a class="work-source-detail" href="${com.example.septic.web.StudioGuideRoutes.route("/images/case-study/redacted/shelby-site-plan-detail-public.png", production)}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Enlarge original plan containing these specifications (opens in a new tab)"><img src="/images/case-study/redacted/shelby-site-plan-detail-public.png" alt="Enlarged original annotations: 1,000-gallon tank, proposed four-bedroom residence and 600 feet of field lines" width="560" height="1210" loading="lazy"></a><p class="work-detail-note">Same source, closer view. The full public excerpt is below.</p><a href="${com.example.septic.web.StudioGuideRoutes.route("/images/case-study/redacted/shelby-site-plan-detail-public.png", production)}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Enlarge the actual Shelby site plan (opens in a new tab)"><img src="/images/case-study/redacted/shelby-site-plan-detail-public.png" alt="Actual anonymized Shelby plan showing the proposed four-bedroom residence, 1,000-gallon tank and 600 feet of field lines" width="560" height="1210" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>Actual county source excerpt · identifying details omitted<br><a href="${com.example.septic.web.StudioGuideRoutes.route("/images/case-study/redacted/shelby-site-plan-detail-public.png", production)}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Enlarge source ↗</a></figcaption></figure><div class="work-evidence__copy"><p class="studio-overline">From the source</p><h2 id="evidence-title">What the plan<br>actually says.</h2><dl class="work-findings"><div><dt>Four bedrooms</dt><dd>The proposed residence label on the drawing.</dd></div><div><dt>1,000-gallon tank</dt><dd>The tank specification recorded on the plan.</dd></div><div><dt>600 feet of field lines</dt><dd>The documented design, not a present-day measurement.</dd></div></dl><p class="studio-fine">This is an approved design, not verification of today's installation or condition.</p>
<a class="studio-text-link" href="#case-boundaries">Read the findings and limitations <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
    <section class="work-limits-banner"><img src="/images/studio/oak-pasture-v1.webp" alt="" width="1672" height="941" loading="lazy"><div class="studio-wrap"><p class="studio-overline">The limits belong in the answer</p><h2>A file has limits.<br>We make them clear.</h2></div></section>
    <section class="work-limits studio-wrap" id="case-boundaries" aria-label="What this case does and does not establish"><div><p class="studio-overline">What the records establish</p><h3>A documented design.</h3><p>The county identified one historical permit and found no repair permits or soil/perc records in its file. That describes the file search, not everything that may have happened on the property.</p></div><div><p class="studio-overline">What remains open</p><h3>The present-day picture.</h3><p>Current tank and field positions, condition and undocumented changes still need field verification.</p><p>The county referred final-inspection questions from that period to Code Enforcement. The returned design is not proof of final installation approval, a passed inspection or a completed sale.</p></div></section>
    <section class="work-explanation studio-wrap" aria-labelledby="explanation-title"><div><p class="studio-overline">The handoff</p><h2 id="explanation-title">The source.<br>And what it means.</h2><p>Keep the original evidence alongside the explanation, with the remaining field questions visible.</p></div><figure><a href="${com.example.septic.web.StudioGuideRoutes.route("/images/case-study/redacted/shelby-brief-findings-public.png", production)}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><img src="/images/case-study/redacted/shelby-brief-findings-public.png" alt="Actual anonymized SepticPath Record Brief findings from the Shelby case" width="835" height="300" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>Actual delivered findings excerpt · <a href="${com.example.septic.web.StudioGuideRoutes.route("/images/case-study/redacted/shelby-brief-findings-public.png", production)}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open full size ↗</a></figcaption></figure></section>
    <section class="work-stories studio-wrap" aria-labelledby="stories-title"><p class="studio-overline">More case stories</p><h2 id="stories-title">Different properties.<br>A clearer path.</h2><ol class="studio-steps">
        <li><span class="studio-steps__number">01</span><div><h3>A historical layout.</h3><p>Roane County, TN · A historical sketch supplied a documented starting point for the tank and field layout.</p></div><a href="${com.example.septic.web.StudioGuideRoutes.route("/septic-record-brief-example/roane/", production)}">Read the story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></li>
        <li><span class="studio-steps__number">02</span><div><h3>Design versus final record.</h3><p>Anderson County, SC · Comparing two source documents revealed different recorded lengths.</p></div><a href="${com.example.septic.web.StudioGuideRoutes.route("/septic-record-brief-example/anderson/", production)}">Read the story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></li>
        <li><span class="studio-steps__number">03</span><div><h3>A revised archive.</h3><p>St. Croix County, WI · A focused three-page extract made the relevant revised records easier to use.</p></div><a href="${com.example.septic.web.StudioGuideRoutes.route("/septic-record-brief-example/st-croix/", production)}">Read the story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></li>
        <li><span class="studio-steps__number">04</span><div><h3>An uncertain old address match.</h3><p>Overton County, TN · Older clues led to a repair file, but missing street-number evidence left the property match unconfirmed.</p></div><a href="${com.example.septic.web.StudioGuideRoutes.route("/septic-record-brief-example/overton/", production)}">Read the story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></li>
        <li><span class="studio-steps__number">05</span><div><h3>The permit. Then the completion record.</h3><p>Williamson County, Tennessee · Can the file show both the approved design and its completion?</p></div><a href="${com.example.septic.web.StudioGuideRoutes.route("/septic-record-brief-example/williamson/", production)}">Read the story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></li>
        <li><span class="studio-steps__number">06</span><div><h3>Before the pool, understand the file.</h3><p>Morgan County, Alabama · Where are the tank and field lines before a pool is planned?</p></div><a href="${com.example.septic.web.StudioGuideRoutes.route("/septic-record-brief-example/morgan/", production)}">Read the story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></li>
        <li><span class="studio-steps__number">07</span><div><h3>A recent claim. An older record.</h3><p>Haverhill, Massachusetts · Does the city file document the reported recent field replacement?</p></div><a href="${com.example.septic.web.StudioGuideRoutes.route("/septic-record-brief-example/haverhill/", production)}">Read the story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></li>
        <li><span class="studio-steps__number">08</span><div><h3>No file found. A clear answer anyway.</h3><p>Cole County, Missouri · Can county records identify an existing tank's location?</p></div><a href="${com.example.septic.web.StudioGuideRoutes.route("/septic-record-brief-example/cole/", production)}">Read the story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></li>
    </ol></section>
    <section class="studio-closing" aria-labelledby="work-next"><img src="/images/studio/oak-pasture-v1.webp" alt="" width="1672" height="941" loading="lazy"><div class="studio-wrap"><p class="studio-overline">Your property's next chapter</p><h2 id="work-next">What's your property's<br>unanswered question?</h2><p>Start with free research. Preview the result before choosing the optional US $29 package.</p><a class="studio-button" href="${com.example.septic.web.StudioGuideRoutes.route("/offer-prep-septic-file-check/", production)}">Ask about my property <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="editorial-start__note">Agency fees are additional at cost, with your approval. No automatic charge.</p></div></section>
</main>
`)
